%X Behavior and short-term memory function were studied in adult rats risen under conditions of partial intraspecies social deprivation. Testing of delayed responses (and emotional state) showed that the partial deprivation of intraspecies communication at the early stage of postnatal ontogeny led not only to disorders of short-term memory in the adult rats but also to behavioral alterations which may be due to impaired development of the regulatory mechanisms of motivation and emotions.
