%J Neurosci Lett
%V 787
%P 136818
%A Ascencio Gutierrez V., Carrillo A. A., Boersma G. J., Tamashiro K. L. K., Moran T. H., Iñiguez S. D., Treesukosol Y.
%K AnimalsMaleRatsAvoidance LearningBody Weight*Fluoxetine/pharmacologyLithium Chloride/pharmacologyRats Sprague-DawleySaccharinTasteFemale*Stress PsychologicalPrenatal Exposure Delayed EffectsAdolescenceCtaChronic variable stressHypophagiaLong-termSSRIcompeting financial interests or personal relationships that could have appearedto influence the work reported in this paper.
%K Fluoxetine
