%T Lactobacillus reuteri effects on maternal separation stress in newborn mice
%D 2021
%8 2021
%J Pediatric Research
%V 90
%N 5
%P 980-988
%A Park E. S., Freeborn J., Venna V. R., Roos S., Rhoads J. M., Liu Y.
%K 5 hydroxytryphtamine receptor 1abeta 2 adrenergic receptorbeta actinbeta glucuronidaseCD200 antigenchemokine receptor CCR2genomic DNAglyceraldehyde 3 phosphate dehydrogenaseinterleukin 1alphaisoetarinekappa opiate receptorkappa opiate receptor 1messenger RNAmetabotropic receptor 1mitogen activated protein kinase 14opiate peptideopiate receptorprodynorphinprostaglandin endoperoxide synthase 2prostaglandin synthasepurinergic P2X4 receptorsodium chlorideunclassified druganimal experimentarticlebrain analysiscomparative studycontrolled studydown regulationfemalegene expressionimmobilization stressLactobacillus reuterimaternal deprivationmaternal stressmouseneonatal stressnewbornnonhumansound analysisultrasonic vocalizationultrasoundupregulationvocalization
%K Mice
