%M rayyan-1166385047
%T H3K9me2 regulation of BDNF expression in the hippocampus and medial prefrontal cortex is involved in the depressive-like phenotype induced by maternal separation in male rats
%D 2021
%8 2021
%J Psychopharmacology
%V 238
%N 10
%P 2801-2813
%A Jiang Z., Zhu Z., Zhao M., Wang W., Li H., Liu D., Pan F.
%K brain derived neurotrophic factorenzyme inhibitorhistone H3histone H3 lysine 9histone methyltransferaseunc 0642unc0642unclassified drugadultanhedoniaanimal cellanimal experimentanimal modelanimal tissueanxietyarticlechronic stresscontrolled studydepressionearly life stresselevated plus maze testepigeneticshippocampushistone methylationimmunohistochemistrylocomotionmalematernal deprivationmedial prefrontal cortexMorris water maze testnonhumanopen field testprotein expressionratreal time polymerase chain reactionspatial memorysucrose preference testWestern blottingWistar rat
%K Rats
%K Hippocampus
%K Phenotype
%K Brain-Derived Neurotrophic Factor
%K Prefrontal Cortex
%X Background: Early life stress (ELS) induces a depressive-like phenotype and increases the risk of depression. Brain‐derived neurotrophic factor (BDNF) has been confirmed to be involved in the pathophysiology of depression. However the mechanism by which ELS alters the epigenetic regulation of BDNF and changes susceptibility to depression has not been fully clarified. Methods: The present study used maternal separation (MS) and chronic unpredicted mild stress (CUMS) to establish an MS animal model and a depressive animal model. We assessed depressive-like behaviours including anhedonia locomotor activity anxiety-like behaviour and spatial memory using the sucrose preference test the open field test the elevated plus maze test and the Morris water maze test. We also investigated BDNF and H3K9me2 expression in the hippocampus and medial prefrontal cortex (mPFC) by immunohistochemistry western blotting and qPCR analysis. Additionally we used Unc0642 a small molecule inhibitor of histone methyltransferase (G9a) as an intervention. Results: The results showed that CUMS induced depressive-like behaviours in rats and resulted in increased H3K9me2 expression and decreased BDNF expression in the hippocampus and mPFC. More importantly adult MS rats experiencing CUMS had more severe depressive behaviours had higher expression of H3K9me2 in the hippocampus and mPFC and had lower expression of BDNF in the hippocampus and mPFC. In addition administration of the G9a inhibitor reversed most of the changes. Conclusions: Our study suggests that ELS changed BDNF and H3K9me2 expression in the rat brain resulting in a depressive-like phenotype.
%R doi:10.1007/s00213-021-05896-7

