%K Deoxycytidine
%K Antidepressive Agents
%X The aim of this study was to investigate the antidepressant activity of 5-aza-2’-deoxycytidine (5-azaD) in the hippocampus in a rat depression model. To develop the model chronic unpredictable stress stimuli and single housing were used to induce depression in rats. Behavior changes in rats were detected using the forced swimming test and sucrose preference test. RT-PCR was used for the quantitative analysis of metabotropic glutamate receptor 2 (mGluR2) and 3(mGluR3). Bisulphite sequencing was used to observe DNA methylation levels of mGluR-2 and -3. Compared with that in the model group the rat behavior evaluation improved significantly in the 5-azaD group. Additionally Bisulphite sequencing showed reduced DNA methylation levels of mGluR-3. Hippocampal mGluR-2 and -3 mRNA levels were up-regulated. 5-azaD can effectively control the symptoms of depression in rats. Its mechanism of action may be associated with decreased expression levels of mGluR-2 and -3 mRNA in hippocampal tissues.
%R doi:

