%K Puberty, Delayed
%K Puberty
%X Chronic crowding of mice during late pregnancy resulted in offspring of lowered birthweights and in the females delayed puberty and altered estrous cycles. Plasma corticosterone in the crowded dams was elevated acutely lending some support to the hypothesis of adrenocortical mediation of prenatal stress effects.
%R doi:10.1007/BF01945561

